            <div xml:id="d115-a7">

                <pb facs="0198" n="124" xml:id="pg124"/>

                <head>[Enclosure G.]</head>
                <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-13"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tuesday, November</hi> 13</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Marsh:</hi> I had another interview and
                    long conversation with Cardinal Antonelli this morning, in reference to the
                    arrest and escape of John H. Surratt. The cardinal gave me the reports of the
                    various officers charged with the investigation of the facts in the case. They
                    certainly show, on the surface, perfect good faith on the part of the Papal
                    authorities, and an earnest desire to arrest the criminal, of whose guilt the
                    cardinal expressed himself fully satisfied. He added that Surratt had, beyond
                    doubt, made good his escape into the Italian territory, and was now, doubtless,
                    at Naples. I write to give you this information, as it may aid your researches.
                    I still think and hope we may catch the fugitive.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUFUS KING.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
